      "data": {
        "text": "**Choosing Authentication**\n\nI'm zeroing in on Firebase Authentication as the external provider. It's a solid choice for straightforward user registration with email and password, and it's easily recognizable in the code. I'm aiming to make sure the code reflects the use of Firebase from the outset.\n\n\n**Defining Implementation Steps**\n\nI've outlined the specific steps to generate the `register_user.py` file. First, I'll create the file. Second, I will write the code, which will use Firebase Authentication to create a new user. The code will explicitly incorporate Firebase-specific identifiers, like the `firebase_admin` import. Finally, it needs to be clearly stated that the user needs to configure their Firebase project and credentials.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789863868201,
          "start": 1789863865624
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc332d18001khoqAJBo3BM25x",
